  "description": "N-1 positive (immortality §6.4: the core speaks N and N-1): a 0.4 core against a frozen 0.3 worker runs create, attach, prefix and a restart-reattach unchanged. The core offers proto_version \"0.3\" toward the 0.3 worker and sends exactly v0.3's messages: every connect and timers carries keepalive_probe_interval (D29), which a 0.3 worker needs to keep a quiet link from blinking (tsb-core #70). This sequence is that half: hello \"0.3\", an ack speaking \"0.3\", and a connect and a later timers carrying the probe key. The live run against the frozen wheel is the rig.",
